# Sentry Onboarding Script Template

This script monitors deploy ref files in `app-interface` and triggers GitHub workflows to kick off Sentry builds for your frontend apps.

---

## 📦 How to Use the Automated Script

### ✅ Prerequisites

1. **Workflow added in the GitHub repo**  
   Ensure your repo has a Sentry GitHub Actions workflow (e.g. `sentry.yml`).  
   Example: [`sentry.yml`](https://github.com/RedHatInsights/insights-remediations-frontend/blob/master/.github/workflows/sentry.yml)

2. **Sentry project is created**  
   If the Sentry project doesn’t exist yet, reach out in `#help-sentry` (super easy to set up).

3. **Sentry plugin is integrated into your app**

   - Add the Sentry plugin in your `fec.config.js`.  
     Example: [fec.config.js](https://github.com/RedHatInsights/insights-remediations-frontend/blob/master/fec.config.js)
   - Install the Sentry wizard to get your DSN and Auth Token:
     ```bash
     npm i @sentry/wizard
     ```
   - You can also retrieve your DSN and Auth Token via the Sentry UI in your project’s settings.

4. **Chrome routes traffic to your app**

   - Make sure your app is included in the [Chrome Sentry config](https://github.com/RedHatInsights/insights-chrome/blob/master/src/utils/sentry.ts)
   - For apps outside the `insights` org, some additional logic may need to be added to route correctly.

5. **(Optional but recommended) Set up a GitLab repo to host and schedule this script**  
   This helps run the script automatically, either on a schedule or in response to app-interface changes. (checkout ExampleGitLabPipeline.txt if you go this route)

---

### 🚀 Running the Script

1. Add your app metadata to `repos.config.js`
2. Ensure you’ve set the required environment variables:
   - `GITHUB_TOKEN` (for triggering GitHub workflows)
   - `SENTRY_AUTH_TOKEN_CHROME` (only if building `insights-chrome`)
3. Run the script:

```bash
cd SentryOnboarding
node index.js
```
